[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944962504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116649#issuecomment-3944962504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116649","id":3944962504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rI1nI","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T14:03:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T14:07:25Z","body":"You should report this to the author of this coroutine utility. This is a bug with the coroutine utility not Godot. The `run` function stays suspended forever in your first code block, because it is awaiting `mSignalTimeOut` which does not get emitted for the removed coroutine object.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944962504/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3948317263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116649#issuecomment-3948317263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116649","id":3948317263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rVopP","user":{"login":"andamiro98cho","id":198149830,"node_id":"U_kgDOC8-Gxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198149830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho","html_url":"https://github.com/andamiro98cho","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T01:18:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T01:24:18Z","body":"> You should report this to the author of this coroutine utility. This is a bug with the coroutine utility not Godot. The `run` function stays suspended forever in your first code block, because it is awaiting `mSignalTimeOut` which does not get emitted for the removed coroutine object.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIt seems there has been some misunderstanding. Even when not using signals and simply awaiting a timeout, if the coroutine is deleted, the same result occurs.\n\nRegardless of whether it is awaiting or not, once a coroutine is deleted it no longer has any meaning. In Lua scripts, all variables used in the coroutine are cleared.\n\nIf a coroutine is deleted while it is awaiting, is this just treated as a memory leak?\n\nIf this is not considered a bug, then GDScript should do one of two things:\n\nEither raise an error when a coroutine is deleted while it is still in an awaiting state,\n\nOr, like other scripting languages, clear all local variables used by the coroutine at the moment it is deleted.\n\nOtherwise, it is impossible to detect the memory leak.\n\nAnd this is not just about a custom coroutine control library… even without such a library, if an object using a coroutine is deleted while it is awaiting, the local variables are not cleaned up.\n\n\n\nBy the way, I created this utility...\n\nAs a coroutine enthusiast, I've done this in every language...\n\nBut I don't understand how GDScript works.\n\nLocal variables are deleted when a coroutine is deleted, not just in Lua scripts, but also in C++/C#.\n\nIn all languages ​​I know, local variables are cleaned up when a coroutine is deleted.\nRegardless of whether await is used within the coroutine or not...\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3948317263/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3950412238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116649#issuecomment-3950412238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116649","id":3950412238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rdoHO","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T09:46:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T09:46:49Z","body":"I missed the fact that those objects actually get freed, it was not very apparent due to it being hidden in the custom linked list. Goes to show why the minimal in MRP is important, thanks for the reduced version in your new issue 👍","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3950412238/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3956737078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116649#issuecomment-3956737078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116649","id":3956737078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7r1wQ2","user":{"login":"andamiro98cho","id":198149830,"node_id":"U_kgDOC8-Gxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198149830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho","html_url":"https://github.com/andamiro98cho","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andamiro98cho/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T04:41:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T04:41:58Z","body":"Finally, the coroutine bug is being fixed… this makes me trust and use the Godot 4 engine even more.\nThanks","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3956737078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]